GPT-6 models: reasoning controls and token limits

Upstream knows only gpt-6-astra, and only in reasoning-effort.ts; every
GPT-6 model fell through to the generic GPT row in tokenLimits.ts (128K
input, 16K output). Per https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models:

- gpt-6-astra, gpt-6.1-sol, gpt-6.1-terra, gpt-6-luna: 1.05M context,
  922K input, 128K output. Added a `/^gpt-6/` row to both tables.
- Sol and Astra accept efforts low…max with medium as default and no
  `none`, so thinking is mandatory. Terra and Luna also accept `none`, so
  thinking is on by default but can be switched off.

gpt-6.1-sol is the default model of the OpenAI API Key preset (0016).

